  <static seed="20" source="Contrib/CCCS/QuantitativeLiteracy/IA_6.1/OpenStax_IA_6.1_53.pg">
    <statement><p>Factor the given polynomial</p>
<p><m>{5x^{3}-15x^{2}+35x-105}=</m> <fillin characters="19" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>If the expression cannot be factored then answer with <alert>prime</alert>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+7\right)\mathopen{}\left(x-3\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>There is a greatest common factor of <m>5</m>.  Start by factoring that out.</p>
<p><m>5({x^{3}-3x^{2}+7x-21})</m></p>
<p>Then we can factor the remaining expression by grouping.</p>
<p><m>5(x^2(x - 3) + 7(x - 3))</m></p>
<p><m>{5\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+7\right)\mathopen{}\left(x-3\right)}</m></p>
</solution>
